    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35027" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕr-hūmānus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very kind</i>, <i>very
				courteous</i>, <i>very polite</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sermo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Q. Fr. 2, 6, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">epistula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 16, 12</span></i>
			. —<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕrhūmānĭter</span></b> , <i>very kindly</i>, <i>very
			politely</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scribere ad aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 7, 8, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
